 lows</strong>, far fewer than the 111 that chance alone would give, and <strong>135 record highs</strong>, close to the 111 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (73). Gulkana's all-time high is 97\u00b0F, on July 10, 1915.","t_chg":"Gulkana has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 78 complete years: Gulkana's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.31\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.11 to +0.50), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1943. Gulkana's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.35\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.18 to +0.53), about +2.9\u00b0F since 1943.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Gulkana's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.18 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 11.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 2022 (22.26 in); the driest, 1969 (5.26 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 0 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}